{"decisions": [{"issue_number": 24, "action": "comment", "comment_body": "Add acceptance criteria. DMMForecaster is probabilistic and must set `self.prob = True` to use Pyro SVI (`model`/`guide` pattern) instead of MSELoss. Required: (1) encoder (inference network / combiner) and decoder (generative network / emitter+transition) as PyroModule sub-modules, (2) `predict()` returns numpy array shape `(n_samples, pred_len, n_features)`, (3) save/load round-trip with safetensors, (4) `fit()` converges on synthetic data in 5 epochs. Reference `probabilistic/_dmm.py` for existing Combiner/Emitter/Transition patterns."}, {"issue_number": 25, "action": "comment", "comment_body": "Add acceptance criteria to ensure a complete Transformer encoder-decoder. Required: (1) positional encoding (sinusoidal or learned) applied to encoder and decoder inputs, (2) multi-head self-attention in encoder and cross-attention in decoder, (3) teacher-forcing support during training via `forward(x, y=None)`, (4) autoregressive `predict()` producing shape `(n_samples, pred_len, n_features)`, (5) save/load round-trip. Follow the `LSTMForecaster` pattern in `stockpy/forecasters/_lstm.py` for forecaster subclass structure."}, {"issue_number": 26, "action": "comment", "comment_body": "Declare dependency on #24. DMMForecaster tests must cover the probabilistic training path in addition to standard deterministic checks. Acceptance criteria: (1) instantiation with `context_len`/`pred_len`, (2) `fit()` runs 5 epochs on synthetic data without error, (3) `predict()` returns shape `(batch, pred_len, features)`, (4) EarlyStopping callback integration, (5) save/load round-trip. Clarify whether `predict()` should return the mean of the posterior predictive or samples."}, {"issue_number": 27, "action": "ok", "comment_body": ""}, {"issue_number": 28, "action": "comment", "comment_body": "Scope is large: `stockpy/base.py` is ~53k tokens and contains many legacy public methods beyond `EncoderDecoderForecaster`. Explicitly scope this issue to `stockpy/base.py` (public methods of `EncoderDecoderForecaster` and its direct helpers only) and all `stockpy/forecasters/_*.py` files. Use `from __future__ import annotations` in every modified file. If base.py annotations exceed one session, split into a separate issue."}, {"issue_number": 29, "action": "ok", "comment_body": ""}, {"issue_number": 30, "action": "ok", "comment_body": ""}, {"issue_number": 31, "action": "ok", "comment_body": ""}]}
